(AI technology was used
in certain scenes during production)

7
00:00:21,760 --> 00:00:22,410
(to help ensure safety during filming)

8
00:00:22,420 --> 00:00:23,020
(and to enhance the quality and
realism of the visuals.)

9
00:00:32,620 --> 00:00:33,920
You finally removed this line.

10
00:00:36,390 --> 00:00:37,570
What were you thinking about just now?

11
00:00:42,660 --> 00:00:43,620
I just regret that

12
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:45,040
if I'd caught Prae that day,

13
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:45,840
(A body was found nearby.)
if I'd caught Prae that day,

14
00:00:45,840 --> 00:00:46,580
(A body was found nearby.)

15
00:00:46,580 --> 00:00:47,800
(A body was found nearby.)
everything would've been over by now.

16
00:00:49,850 --> 00:00:50,560
By the way,

17
00:00:50,960 --> 00:00:52,050
I've never asked you this.

18
00:00:53,530 --> 00:00:54,520
After this case,

19
00:00:55,370 --> 00:00:56,100
what are you going to do?

20
00:00:57,500 --> 00:00:58,470
Do you want to go to Bangkok?

21
00:00:59,210 --> 00:01:00,190
Or would you rather stay here?

22
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:03,990
Can we focus on the case first?

23
00:01:06,280 --> 00:01:08,220
Can I focus on recharging first?

24
00:01:14,040 --> 00:01:15,270
Inspector, something terrible happened.

25
00:01:17,270 --> 00:01:18,720
Prae abducted Dr. Jirat.

26
00:01:59,320 --> 00:02:04,220
=Nour=
(WeTV Original)

27
00:02:10,370 --> 00:02:11,090
Look carefully.

28
00:02:11,810 --> 00:02:12,660
Yeah, I know.

29
00:02:17,690 --> 00:02:18,350
Give it to me.

30
00:02:19,320 --> 00:02:19,740
Hey!

31
00:02:20,690 --> 00:02:21,380
That's my flashlight.

32
00:02:47,410 --> 00:02:48,070
Are you done?

33
00:03:08,390 --> 00:03:09,900
What time did Dr. Jirat disappear?

34
00:03:13,590 --> 00:03:14,330
Around

35
00:03:14,570 --> 00:03:15,270
early evening.

36
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:18,600
And what was Dr. Ji doing here?

37
00:03:20,020 --> 00:03:20,630
Uh...

38
00:03:32,950 --> 00:03:33,480
Well...

39
00:03:34,350 --> 00:03:35,580
Dr. Ji came to drop me off.

40
00:03:36,650 --> 00:03:37,650
And how do you know

41
00:03:37,830 --> 00:03:38,740
that Prae is the culprit?

42
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:42,070
Can you tell me
everything that happened?

43
00:03:44,930 --> 00:03:45,380
Sure.

44
00:03:49,490 --> 00:03:50,950
After Dr. Ji dropped me off,

45
00:03:53,140 --> 00:03:54,320
we said goodbye.

46
00:03:56,910 --> 00:03:58,370
I was about to go inside,

47
00:04:00,260 --> 00:04:00,860
but

48
00:04:01,930 --> 00:04:03,320
I came back out
to take another look at him.

49
00:04:10,370 --> 00:04:11,120
I saw that...

50
00:04:14,050 --> 00:04:14,920
And after that,

51
00:04:15,270 --> 00:04:16,430
Prae dragged Dr. Ji away.

52
00:04:18,760 --> 00:04:19,190
Doctor!

53
00:04:22,350 --> 00:04:22,760
Doctor!

54
00:04:23,730 --> 00:04:24,110
Dr. Ji!

55
00:04:29,590 --> 00:04:30,010
Doctor!

56
00:04:31,680 --> 00:04:32,120
Why

57
00:04:33,060 --> 00:04:34,590
would Prae do this to Dr. Ji?

58
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:40,010
And have you or Dr. Ji

59
00:04:40,010 --> 00:04:42,530
ever spoken to Prae
or known her personally?

60
00:04:43,930 --> 00:04:46,990
I've never seen Dr. Ji
and Prae being close before.

61
00:04:51,130 --> 00:04:51,720
But

62
00:04:52,870 --> 00:04:53,880
on Valentine's Day,

63
00:04:55,190 --> 00:04:57,510
I saw Prae bring the doctor a gift.

64
00:04:58,500 --> 00:04:59,090
Ji.

65
00:04:59,810 --> 00:05:00,230
Yes?

66
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:03,860
Thank you.

67
00:05:04,300 --> 00:05:05,030
Doctor.

68
00:05:06,370 --> 00:05:07,270
Anything else?

69
00:05:18,320 --> 00:05:20,290
I saw Prae walking away
with a bag of blood,

70
00:05:22,540 --> 00:05:23,550
and she happened to run into me.

71
00:05:24,190 --> 00:05:24,650
Excuse me.

72
00:05:25,310 --> 00:05:26,210
Where are you taking that bag of blood?

73
00:05:26,480 --> 00:05:27,410
She was acting suspiciously.

74
00:05:29,260 --> 00:05:29,920
And then she

75
00:05:30,140 --> 00:05:31,390
threatened me not to tell anyone.

76
00:05:34,870 --> 00:05:36,270
But what bothers me is

77
00:05:37,650 --> 00:05:38,970
she squeezed my arm really hard.

78
00:05:38,970 --> 00:05:39,190
Ouch!

79
00:05:40,100 --> 00:05:40,750
So hard that

80
00:05:41,460 --> 00:05:42,530
my whole body hurt.

81
00:05:42,670 --> 00:05:42,980
Ow!

82
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:46,720
It was like she wasn't human.

83
00:05:49,470 --> 00:05:50,950
Could Prae be trying to
silence everyone?

84
00:05:54,140 --> 00:05:54,920
Possibly.

85
00:05:56,240 --> 00:05:58,780
She probably didn't want Chita
telling anyone about this.

86
00:06:00,080 --> 00:06:00,600
Or

87
00:06:03,030 --> 00:06:04,490
maybe she's trying to
silence Dr. Ji too.

88
00:06:11,440 --> 00:06:12,440
Did all of this

89
00:06:15,110 --> 00:06:16,450
happen because of me?

90
00:06:19,500 --> 00:06:21,220
You really can save Dr. Ji, right?

91
00:06:24,630 --> 00:06:25,760
Thank you for the information,

92
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:26,540
Chita.

93
00:06:27,490 --> 00:06:28,870
We'll be leaving now.

94
00:06:30,790 --> 00:06:31,430
Let's go.

95
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:48,750
Hello.

96
00:06:49,960 --> 00:06:50,460
Uh...

97
00:06:50,770 --> 00:06:53,060
Inspector, you need
today's records, right?

98
00:06:53,490 --> 00:06:53,920
Yes.

99
00:06:55,330 --> 00:06:58,440
Actually, four bags of type O blood
were withdrawn that day.

100
00:06:58,440 --> 00:07:00,120
I entered the records myself.

101
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,140
Was Prae there that day?

102
00:07:02,900 --> 00:07:03,590
No.

103
00:07:03,950 --> 00:07:05,240
She had taken the day off.

104
00:07:06,140 --> 00:07:07,270
But actually, every day,

105
00:07:07,270 --> 00:07:09,480
we check the blood inventory
at the blood bank

106
00:07:09,710 --> 00:07:10,580
as part of our routine.

107
00:07:12,460 --> 00:07:14,420
But I'll go check it again for you.

108
00:07:15,240 --> 00:07:15,820
Thank you.

109
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:32,160
(So Prae was going to
take the blood to Tee that day.)

110
00:07:42,650 --> 00:07:44,240
One bag really is missing.

111
00:07:45,830 --> 00:07:47,910
What's going on right now, Inspector?

112
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:49,620
What does Prae have to do with this?

113
00:07:51,070 --> 00:07:53,220
If I find anything,
I'll let you know right away.

114
00:07:54,050 --> 00:07:55,800
But if you see Prae
or manage to contact her,

115
00:07:55,800 --> 00:07:57,910
please contact us as soon as possible.

116
00:07:59,340 --> 00:08:00,500
Thank you for your cooperation.

117
00:08:01,300 --> 00:08:01,720
Sure.

118
00:08:07,690 --> 00:08:08,730
It really is Dr. Ji's blood.

119
00:08:09,610 --> 00:08:12,050
But this is strange,
Dr. Ji's blood trail ends in the woods.

120
00:08:13,090 --> 00:08:14,970
If Prae dragged Dr. Ji into the woods,

121
00:08:15,810 --> 00:08:17,360
why is there no blood trail?

122
00:08:19,770 --> 00:08:21,190
Or was Prae trying to
destroy the evidence

123
00:08:21,560 --> 00:08:22,760
of where she took Dr. Ji?

124
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:25,510
But why would she do that?

125
00:08:28,220 --> 00:08:29,000
Like you said,

126
00:08:29,880 --> 00:08:31,360
Dr. Ji might know that Prae is a Nour.

127
00:08:32,900 --> 00:08:34,220
But I don't understand

128
00:08:35,270 --> 00:08:36,620
why she had to take Dr. Ji.

129
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:40,240
Why not kill him and
leave his body like the others?

130
00:08:43,450 --> 00:08:44,680
Then I'll go see Tangme.

131
00:08:44,990 --> 00:08:46,250
I'll have her trace Prae's phone.

132
00:08:47,070 --> 00:08:47,490
Okay.

133
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:49,850
I think I'll call Panin.

134
00:08:56,620 --> 00:08:57,260
(Hello, Panin.)

135
00:08:57,310 --> 00:08:58,050
(Where are you right now?)

136
00:08:58,770 --> 00:09:00,020
Oh, I'm at the university right now.

137
00:09:00,050 --> 00:09:00,610
What's up?

138
00:09:01,120 --> 00:09:02,090
(Who are you with right now?)

139
00:09:05,020 --> 00:09:06,230
- What's Prae doing here?
- You scared me!

140
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:07,560
(Prae?)

141
00:09:08,630 --> 00:09:09,620
Prae is with you right now?

142
00:09:10,250 --> 00:09:10,600
Yes.

143
00:09:11,130 --> 00:09:12,220
She's talking to Rain about something.

144
00:09:12,940 --> 00:09:13,540
(Panin.)

145
00:09:13,540 --> 00:09:14,650
(Listen to me carefully.)

146
00:09:15,060 --> 00:09:17,060
(Prae is dangerous.)

147
00:09:17,700 --> 00:09:19,330
(Get Rain away from Prae right now.)

148
00:09:19,610 --> 00:09:20,410
How is she dangerous?

149
00:09:21,140 --> 00:09:22,070
What happened?

150
00:09:22,260 --> 00:09:23,190
I'll explain later.

151
00:09:23,420 --> 00:09:24,240
But right now,

152
00:09:24,700 --> 00:09:25,780
Rain isn't safe.

153
00:09:26,050 --> 00:09:27,980
Panin, get Rain away from her now.

154
00:09:28,440 --> 00:09:29,080
And

155
00:09:29,130 --> 00:09:29,750
(don't let Prae know)

156
00:09:30,100 --> 00:09:30,930
(that I called you.)

157
00:09:30,930 --> 00:09:31,490
Okay.

158
00:09:34,140 --> 00:09:34,650
Oh, really?

159
00:09:34,650 --> 00:09:35,120
Rain.

160
00:09:35,830 --> 00:09:36,570
I need to talk to you.

161
00:09:37,750 --> 00:09:38,150
About what?

162
00:09:39,100 --> 00:09:40,480
Seriously, I need to
talk to you right now.

163
00:09:41,190 --> 00:09:41,460
Let’s go.

164
00:09:42,920 --> 00:09:43,430
See you later.

165
00:09:43,960 --> 00:09:45,340
What the heck is wrong with you?

166
00:09:46,420 --> 00:09:46,760
Shoot!

167
00:09:47,540 --> 00:09:47,980
That hurts!

168
00:09:49,930 --> 00:09:50,610
What the heck is wrong with you?

169
00:09:51,970 --> 00:09:52,850
I'm saving you right now.

170
00:09:53,350 --> 00:09:54,140
From what?

171
00:09:54,890 --> 00:09:55,970
You didn't even want to
talk to me yesterday.

172
00:10:00,820 --> 00:10:01,410
I had to.

173
00:10:02,810 --> 00:10:04,170
Otherwise, Prae might've done
something to you.

174
00:10:10,900 --> 00:10:11,600
James said

175
00:10:12,610 --> 00:10:13,320
Prae is dangerous.

176
00:10:14,860 --> 00:10:15,890
That's why I had to
get you out of there.

177
00:10:22,460 --> 00:10:23,040
Dangerous?

178
00:10:24,740 --> 00:10:25,440
How is she dangerous?

179
00:10:28,070 --> 00:10:28,850
I don't know.

180
00:10:31,240 --> 00:10:32,220
He didn't get a chance to tell me.

181
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:34,040
So, I had to save you first.

182
00:10:40,990 --> 00:10:41,750
Thanks, I guess.

183
00:12:13,860 --> 00:12:14,490
Where's Prae?

184
00:12:15,480 --> 00:12:16,450
What happened, James?

185
00:12:17,710 --> 00:12:18,380
Prae is a Nour.

186
00:12:18,880 --> 00:12:20,000
Prae abducted Dr. Jirat.

187
00:12:22,340 --> 00:12:22,800
That's not true.

188
00:12:23,310 --> 00:12:23,860
No way.

189
00:12:25,160 --> 00:12:26,370
Then my brother isn't safe either.

190
00:12:27,520 --> 00:12:28,460
You have to find him.

191
00:12:29,230 --> 00:12:30,140
What if something

192
00:12:30,760 --> 00:12:31,420
happens to my brother?

193
00:12:32,400 --> 00:12:33,040
Don't worry.

194
00:12:33,590 --> 00:12:34,590
Dr. Ji will be safe.

195
00:12:35,470 --> 00:12:37,140
We'll do everything we can to find him.

196
00:12:38,170 --> 00:12:38,990
But you guys

197
00:12:39,540 --> 00:12:40,660
need to cooperate with us too.

198
00:12:42,210 --> 00:12:43,090
What was Prae doing here?

199
00:12:43,660 --> 00:12:44,260
And what did you talk about?

200
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:46,670
I

201
00:12:46,720 --> 00:12:48,890
saw Prae looking through Tee's locker.

202
00:12:49,940 --> 00:12:52,130
Looks like she came for something
Tee bought before he died.

203
00:12:54,170 --> 00:12:56,330
That means Prae probably destroyed
the evidence and fled.

204
00:12:58,960 --> 00:12:59,770
I don't understand.

205
00:13:00,660 --> 00:13:02,230
I thought Prae was here to hurt someone.

206
00:13:03,460 --> 00:13:04,460
If she was planning to escape,

207
00:13:05,750 --> 00:13:07,070
why did Prae say that

208
00:13:07,660 --> 00:13:08,530
when she confronted us?

209
00:13:09,220 --> 00:13:11,400
We still need to keep
tracking Prae's movements.

210
00:13:12,160 --> 00:13:14,540
And we can't rule out
any possibilities yet.

211
00:13:15,800 --> 00:13:16,630
I'll help investigate too.

212
00:13:16,770 --> 00:13:17,130
Hey.

213
00:13:18,640 --> 00:13:20,270
I think you should leave
this to the police.

214
00:13:20,640 --> 00:13:22,760
If Prae really is a Nour,
there's nothing you can do anyway.

215
00:13:23,190 --> 00:13:24,000
Stay out of this.

216
00:13:24,800 --> 00:13:25,490
That's my brother!

217
00:13:25,930 --> 00:13:26,880
Panin, calm down

218
00:13:27,160 --> 00:13:27,810
and listen to me.

219
00:13:28,390 --> 00:13:29,210
Go home first.

220
00:13:31,260 --> 00:13:32,070
As for Dr. Ji,

221
00:13:32,270 --> 00:13:33,130
we'll handle it.

222
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:35,020
I'll find Prae as soon as possible

223
00:13:35,360 --> 00:13:36,400
and rescue your brother.

224
00:13:36,900 --> 00:13:37,990
Please let me help find my brother.

225
00:13:38,650 --> 00:13:39,230
Go home.

226
00:13:40,120 --> 00:13:41,340
You won't be any help coming with us.

227
00:13:42,120 --> 00:13:43,060
Go home with your friend.

228
00:13:43,190 --> 00:13:43,550
Go.

229
00:13:43,680 --> 00:13:44,460
Ken.

230
00:13:44,750 --> 00:13:45,250
Go.

231
00:13:53,460 --> 00:13:54,990
(Suspect)

232
00:13:54,990 --> 00:13:56,630
(CCTV Evidence)

233
00:13:56,630 --> 00:13:58,070
(Ms. Prabhaporn Phanthananthakun)
All the documents were forged.

234
00:13:58,070 --> 00:13:58,870
(Previous Information)

235
00:13:58,870 --> 00:14:00,310
Earlier, I found evidence that

236
00:14:00,310 --> 00:14:02,570
(Suspect)
Prae was born and raised in an orphanage

237
00:14:03,030 --> 00:14:04,230
in Amnat Charoen.
But when I sent someone to investigate,

238
00:14:04,350 --> 00:14:05,050
we found that

239
00:14:05,050 --> 00:14:06,570
the orphanage never actually existed.

240
00:14:08,800 --> 00:14:09,710
Thank you so much, Tangme.

241
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:11,510
I'm sorry, Inspector.

242
00:14:11,980 --> 00:14:13,430
The more I search,
the less I seem to find.

243
00:14:14,310 --> 00:14:16,350
Both her ID card and surname

244
00:14:16,350 --> 00:14:17,790
were changed four years ago.

245
00:14:18,310 --> 00:14:20,830
Dr. Ji's last known location
was Chita's dorm.

246
00:14:21,720 --> 00:14:24,120
After that, there was no signal
or anything else.

247
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:27,140
I want to try something.

248
00:14:28,080 --> 00:14:28,630
Tangme.

249
00:14:29,360 --> 00:14:31,110
You can trace
the other party's signal, right?

250
00:14:31,490 --> 00:14:32,360
I'll try.

251
00:14:33,350 --> 00:14:34,540
Who are you going to call, Inspector?

252
00:14:34,830 --> 00:14:35,870
I'm going to call Prae.

253
00:14:35,960 --> 00:14:37,300
If I call from Tee's phone,

254
00:14:37,300 --> 00:14:38,590
Prae definitely won't hang up.

255
00:14:38,670 --> 00:14:39,700
It should buy us enough time

256
00:14:39,700 --> 00:14:40,880
for Tangme to trace the signal.

257
00:14:41,530 --> 00:14:42,540
I doubt it.

258
00:14:58,460 --> 00:14:59,080
Inspector.

259
00:15:38,400 --> 00:15:39,070
Hey, old man.

260
00:15:42,660 --> 00:15:43,400
I think

261
00:15:44,230 --> 00:15:45,430
GPS alone

262
00:15:45,580 --> 00:15:46,840
should be enough.

263
00:15:47,550 --> 00:15:48,780
I'm just double-checking.

264
00:15:50,600 --> 00:15:51,370
Whatever.

265
00:15:56,340 --> 00:15:56,800
Ready?

266
00:15:57,800 --> 00:15:58,100
Ready.

267
00:16:15,490 --> 00:16:16,290
What are you doing?

268
00:16:18,060 --> 00:16:18,390
Not telling you.

269
00:16:23,060 --> 00:16:23,950
Fine, I won't tease you.

270
00:16:26,020 --> 00:16:27,920
I checked the chats
between Prae and Tee.

271
00:16:28,900 --> 00:16:30,340
Prae told Tee she'd finished
withdrawing the blood

272
00:16:30,340 --> 00:16:31,260
and was about to bring it to him.

273
00:16:38,340 --> 00:16:39,500
But since Prae was abducted,

274
00:16:39,990 --> 00:16:41,480
she couldn't meet Tee.

275
00:16:41,830 --> 00:16:43,190
Someone attacked me from behind.

276
00:16:44,470 --> 00:16:45,580
And I don't remember
anything after that.

277
00:16:47,110 --> 00:16:49,040
Judging by the timing and the messages,

278
00:16:50,190 --> 00:16:51,390
I think Prae was telling the truth

279
00:16:51,800 --> 00:16:52,740
about being abducted.

280
00:16:57,360 --> 00:16:58,510
Then after a while,

281
00:16:59,380 --> 00:17:01,000
Tee replied that
he was coming to see her.

282
00:17:02,350 --> 00:17:04,330
But Prae never replied.

283
00:17:10,950 --> 00:17:11,930
Wait! Wait!

284
00:17:12,680 --> 00:17:13,340
Let me come with you.

285
00:17:20,200 --> 00:17:20,530
Prae.

286
00:17:21,270 --> 00:17:21,910
I already have a ride.

287
00:17:24,090 --> 00:17:24,960
Please let me come with you.

288
00:17:28,520 --> 00:17:29,380
I think right now

289
00:17:30,230 --> 00:17:31,810
your friend is one of the suspects.

290
00:17:33,390 --> 00:17:34,200
Dr. Ji?

291
00:17:35,430 --> 00:17:36,250
Please believe me.

292
00:17:36,890 --> 00:17:38,250
Dr. Ji isn't a Nour.

293
00:17:38,820 --> 00:17:40,440
He might be a Nour
and just never told you.

294
00:17:41,820 --> 00:17:42,580
Or

295
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:44,560
he could be behind Tee's death.

296
00:17:46,530 --> 00:17:47,690
Whatever you think.

297
00:17:48,950 --> 00:17:50,970
I can't stop you
from thinking that anyway.

298
00:17:51,640 --> 00:17:52,570
You're so stubborn.

299
00:17:55,230 --> 00:17:56,110
You're even more stubborn than I am.

300
00:17:57,190 --> 00:17:58,920
We already have
the culprit's GPS location,

301
00:17:59,450 --> 00:18:01,080
and you're still using a map.

302
00:18:04,260 --> 00:18:05,420
If changing something
makes things better,

303
00:18:05,800 --> 00:18:06,670
then you should change it.

304
00:18:07,340 --> 00:18:09,340
You don't have to
act like an old man all the time.

305
00:18:10,800 --> 00:18:12,040
And this car,

306
00:18:12,490 --> 00:18:13,620
when are you going to replace it, huh?

307
00:18:17,980 --> 00:18:19,160
I used to think

308
00:18:19,510 --> 00:18:20,550
I wanted to ride in a sports car.

309
00:18:21,240 --> 00:18:22,780
But I've changed my mind now.

310
00:18:26,040 --> 00:18:27,310
Even though this car is old,

311
00:18:27,770 --> 00:18:29,000
the fuel gauge doesn't work,

312
00:18:30,010 --> 00:18:32,200
and it can only go up to
80 kilometers per hour,

313
00:18:33,030 --> 00:18:34,190
I still like it.

314
00:18:41,080 --> 00:18:42,280
But you're wrong about one thing.

315
00:18:43,720 --> 00:18:45,940
My car can go faster
than 80 kilometers per hour.

316
00:18:46,820 --> 00:18:47,770
Hey!

317
00:19:04,330 --> 00:19:06,110
I thought you didn't
want to talk to me anymore.

318
00:19:07,050 --> 00:19:08,300
You came in and
left the door open again.

319
00:19:09,290 --> 00:19:09,640
Rain.

320
00:19:13,770 --> 00:19:14,520
Jeez.

321
00:19:15,040 --> 00:19:15,510
What?

322
00:19:16,220 --> 00:19:17,070
Did you miss me?

323
00:19:18,080 --> 00:19:19,320
You called me like ten times.

324
00:19:22,020 --> 00:19:23,750
I just didn't know
who else to talk to about this.

325
00:19:26,300 --> 00:19:27,130
Jeez.

326
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:29,390
Move over.

327
00:19:35,070 --> 00:19:36,310
Don't overthink it.

328
00:19:37,640 --> 00:19:39,940
I'm sure James can find your brother.

329
00:19:40,360 --> 00:19:41,260
He's really good at what he does.

330
00:19:41,330 --> 00:19:42,040
And he's huge.

331
00:19:42,890 --> 00:19:43,470
He's ripped too.

332
00:19:44,720 --> 00:19:45,460
I

333
00:19:45,720 --> 00:19:46,720
hope so.

334
00:19:51,550 --> 00:19:53,070
I'm scared that if my mom finds out,

335
00:19:54,520 --> 00:19:56,200
her illness will flare up again.

336
00:19:57,290 --> 00:19:58,200
And I feel like

337
00:20:00,020 --> 00:20:01,280
I can't help anyone right now.

338
00:20:02,350 --> 00:20:03,580
Not my brother,

339
00:20:04,170 --> 00:20:05,110
not my mom.

340
00:20:06,560 --> 00:20:07,080
Nin.

341
00:20:07,940 --> 00:20:08,970
Listen to me.

342
00:20:09,740 --> 00:20:11,370
You're just a college student

343
00:20:12,140 --> 00:20:12,660
who

344
00:20:13,130 --> 00:20:14,340
goes to class every day

345
00:20:14,760 --> 00:20:15,860
just to avoid getting a W.

346
00:20:16,510 --> 00:20:17,420
And besides,

347
00:20:17,640 --> 00:20:19,640
you're not a police officer.

348
00:20:19,780 --> 00:20:21,210
It's not your job.

349
00:20:21,600 --> 00:20:23,310
You're putting too much
pressure on yourself.

350
00:20:28,450 --> 00:20:29,710
You're too stressed out.

351
00:20:34,030 --> 00:20:35,390
But I'm sorry that I

352
00:20:36,880 --> 00:20:37,820
distanced myself from you.

353
00:20:39,070 --> 00:20:39,960
Dang.

354
00:20:41,750 --> 00:20:43,520
Whenever I feel bad, I need you.

355
00:20:45,080 --> 00:20:45,940
I'm so selfish.

356
00:20:46,350 --> 00:20:47,180
Yeah.

357
00:20:48,770 --> 00:20:50,460
You know I was hurt, right?

358
00:20:54,510 --> 00:20:55,580
But I'm kind of embarrassed too.

359
00:20:57,410 --> 00:20:57,960
What's in your head?

360
00:20:58,570 --> 00:20:58,900
Well,

361
00:21:00,030 --> 00:21:01,440
whenever you have a problem,

362
00:21:02,800 --> 00:21:04,140
I'm the first person you think of.

363
00:21:06,220 --> 00:21:08,200
Who wouldn't be embarrassed?
Are you crazy?

364
00:21:15,680 --> 00:21:16,330
Trust me.

365
00:21:16,530 --> 00:21:17,510
Your brother will be safe.

366
00:21:18,810 --> 00:21:19,370
Yeah.

367
00:21:20,900 --> 00:21:21,590
You think too much.

368
00:21:23,250 --> 00:21:24,060
Can I borrow this?

369
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:25,470
Go ahead.

370
00:21:25,470 --> 00:21:26,730
Read whatever you want.

371
00:21:28,790 --> 00:21:29,440
Jeez.

372
00:21:30,490 --> 00:21:31,720
I have to close the door again.

373
00:21:37,250 --> 00:21:38,220
Which volume did you buy?

374
00:21:40,990 --> 00:21:43,040
I don't know. I just bought it to read.
You know I like reading.

375
00:21:54,400 --> 00:21:55,800
On the first day of rebirth,

376
00:21:58,110 --> 00:21:59,630
it feels like you're burning up inside,

377
00:22:00,760 --> 00:22:02,520
but sometimes you're so cold
that your whole body trembles.

378
00:22:04,980 --> 00:22:06,600
Did you feel this way
when you first became a Nour?

379
00:22:12,220 --> 00:22:12,620
Hey!

380
00:22:15,550 --> 00:22:16,340
I...

381
00:22:17,150 --> 00:22:17,910
don't remember.

382
00:22:18,970 --> 00:22:20,060
It was a long time ago.

383
00:22:23,310 --> 00:22:24,660
And it says here too.

384
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:27,350
Prae is my true love.

385
00:22:28,940 --> 00:22:30,190
She made me die,

386
00:22:31,260 --> 00:22:33,000
so I could be reborn as a better person.

387
00:22:34,950 --> 00:22:35,560
What does that mean?

388
00:22:36,860 --> 00:22:38,370
Do you have to be true loves
to become a Nour?

389
00:22:43,050 --> 00:22:44,310
You have to bite into the heart.

390
00:22:47,800 --> 00:22:49,160
But if that person isn't your true love,

391
00:22:50,540 --> 00:22:51,590
they'll die instantly.

392
00:22:53,700 --> 00:22:54,460
They'll die?

393
00:22:56,820 --> 00:22:57,970
Then who turned you into a Nour?

394
00:23:04,090 --> 00:23:05,530
And if one day I'm dying,

395
00:23:06,790 --> 00:23:08,080
would you bite me
and turn me into a Nour?

396
00:23:15,100 --> 00:23:16,870
I actually want to
bite you to prove our true love.

397
00:23:18,590 --> 00:23:19,990
But now that I think about it,

398
00:23:22,870 --> 00:23:23,570
maybe not.

399
00:23:25,470 --> 00:23:26,280
No matter what,

400
00:23:27,960 --> 00:23:29,690
please don't turn me into a Nour.

401
00:23:34,600 --> 00:23:36,120
I won't turn you into a Nour.

402
00:23:36,890 --> 00:23:37,830
I promise.

403
00:23:42,020 --> 00:23:42,890
I think

404
00:23:43,750 --> 00:23:44,740
this thing with Prae

405
00:23:45,800 --> 00:23:47,360
might be more dangerous than we thought.

406
00:23:48,220 --> 00:23:48,890
You...

407
00:23:56,690 --> 00:23:57,260
Hey, you.

408
00:23:58,470 --> 00:23:59,060
A rainbow.

409
00:24:00,350 --> 00:24:00,980
A rainbow?

410
00:24:10,350 --> 00:24:11,180
It really is a rainbow.

411
00:24:15,180 --> 00:24:16,500
But the rainbow I see

412
00:24:18,590 --> 00:24:19,810
isn't that beautiful.

413
00:24:21,320 --> 00:24:22,300
Then this time,

414
00:24:22,880 --> 00:24:24,390
look at it carefully.

415
00:24:25,500 --> 00:24:26,160
Why?

416
00:24:28,020 --> 00:24:29,450
Because I'll explain it to you

417
00:24:30,230 --> 00:24:31,390
what each color looks like.

418
00:24:36,470 --> 00:24:37,380
At the very top

419
00:24:38,250 --> 00:24:39,040
is red.

420
00:24:39,760 --> 00:24:40,520
Can you see it?

421
00:24:45,590 --> 00:24:46,380
Red,

422
00:24:47,020 --> 00:24:48,290
like your cheeks

423
00:24:49,630 --> 00:24:50,450
when you

424
00:24:50,890 --> 00:24:51,720
blush at me.

425
00:24:52,820 --> 00:24:53,490
No way.

426
00:24:54,490 --> 00:24:55,740
Red is more like

427
00:24:56,570 --> 00:24:59,230
when I choke you
until you can't breathe.

428
00:25:01,730 --> 00:25:03,090
You're not romantic at all, Inspector.

429
00:25:04,360 --> 00:25:06,340
Try looking at it with your heart.

430
00:25:09,560 --> 00:25:10,200
Close your eyes.

431
00:25:12,220 --> 00:25:12,880
Close your eyes.

432
00:25:13,710 --> 00:25:14,760
I'll close mine with you.

433
00:25:25,300 --> 00:25:26,200
Next

434
00:25:26,820 --> 00:25:27,710
is orange.

435
00:25:29,890 --> 00:25:31,810
Like the color of the evening sky.

436
00:25:34,780 --> 00:25:36,050
Then yellow,

437
00:25:37,420 --> 00:25:39,190
like the color of your headlights.

438
00:25:41,820 --> 00:25:43,000
Then green,

439
00:25:45,400 --> 00:25:47,030
like the color of my motorcycle.

440
00:25:48,820 --> 00:25:50,410
As for indigo and blue,

441
00:25:51,600 --> 00:25:53,520
they're like the daytime sky.

442
00:25:55,780 --> 00:25:56,640
And at the very bottom

443
00:25:57,680 --> 00:25:58,620
is violet,

444
00:26:01,060 --> 00:26:02,420
like the color of the sky

445
00:26:03,530 --> 00:26:04,670
when winter comes.

446
00:26:13,860 --> 00:26:14,560
Thank you.

447
00:26:20,320 --> 00:26:22,220
Even though I can't see
the colors of the rainbow,

448
00:26:23,790 --> 00:26:25,390
I can still feel

449
00:26:26,120 --> 00:26:27,190
how beautiful it is

450
00:26:29,000 --> 00:26:30,320
from your smile.

451
00:26:33,900 --> 00:26:34,880
All this time,

452
00:26:36,880 --> 00:26:38,830
I never knew
how many colors a rainbow had.

453
00:26:39,000 --> 00:26:42,470
♪Bound by fate we cannot break♪

454
00:26:42,470 --> 00:26:45,630
♪Silent thoughts we both share♪

455
00:26:46,160 --> 00:26:52,040
♪Found a light no dark can shake♪

456
00:26:52,900 --> 00:26:59,040
♪We make a wish toward rainbow's end♪

457
00:27:00,500 --> 00:27:06,260
♪Chase the dream beyond the bend♪

458
00:27:06,320 --> 00:27:08,520
♪I'll make sure
you see it with your own eyes.♪

459
00:27:08,520 --> 00:27:12,340
♪Though this hope
can never reach the ground♪

460
00:27:12,340 --> 00:27:14,990
I'll drive you somewhere
you can see a rainbow up close.

461
00:27:15,990 --> 00:27:18,020
Close enough to see all seven colors.

462
00:27:18,750 --> 00:27:19,540
I promise.

463
00:27:49,760 --> 00:27:55,340
♪Wish stays locked inside my heart♪

464
00:27:56,970 --> 00:28:02,670
♪Colored memories never depart♪

465
00:28:04,450 --> 00:28:10,290
♪Love that's doomed yet stole my heart♪

466
00:28:11,950 --> 00:28:17,780
♪Love that's doomed yet stole my heart♪

467
00:28:22,630 --> 00:28:23,350
Wait.

468
00:28:24,170 --> 00:28:24,850
What is it?

469
00:28:26,050 --> 00:28:27,350
Prae's location is moving faster.

470
00:28:28,120 --> 00:28:29,190
Then it suddenly stops.

471
00:28:29,780 --> 00:28:30,660
It keeps moving around.

472
00:28:33,970 --> 00:28:34,980
Like she's running from something.

473
00:28:36,860 --> 00:28:37,980
Did we lose Prae's location?

474
00:28:38,880 --> 00:28:39,520
No.

475
00:28:40,930 --> 00:28:42,480
But Prae is heading somewhere else.

476
00:29:16,720 --> 00:29:18,660
Why did Prae want to meet us here?

477
00:29:19,300 --> 00:29:20,270
If I had to guess,

478
00:29:20,400 --> 00:29:21,770
she probably came back to get something.

479
00:29:24,070 --> 00:29:24,880
Let's go.

480
00:30:24,440 --> 00:30:25,310
Wait! Wait!

481
00:30:26,140 --> 00:30:26,860
Let me come with you.

482
00:30:30,410 --> 00:30:30,890
Prae.

483
00:30:31,480 --> 00:30:32,350
I already have a ride.

484
00:30:34,390 --> 00:30:35,250
Please let me come with you.

485
00:30:53,370 --> 00:30:54,560
(Tee)

486
00:30:56,570 --> 00:30:57,100
Tee.

487
00:30:57,600 --> 00:30:58,020
Prae.

488
00:31:18,970 --> 00:31:19,460
Let go!

489
00:31:25,060 --> 00:31:25,620
Ow!

490
00:32:15,290 --> 00:32:17,040
(Pathology Department)

491
00:32:56,190 --> 00:32:56,940
Dad.

492
00:33:06,480 --> 00:33:07,660
You scum!

493
00:33:08,490 --> 00:33:10,530
You killed my dad, didn't you?

494
00:33:10,860 --> 00:33:11,500
Huh?

495
00:33:11,870 --> 00:33:12,460
Huh?

496
00:33:12,710 --> 00:33:13,440
You scum!

497
00:33:13,550 --> 00:33:14,770
You scum!

498
00:33:19,760 --> 00:33:21,010
You scum!

499
00:33:21,360 --> 00:33:22,160
You scum, Chita!

500
00:33:48,900 --> 00:33:50,070
You scum!

501
00:33:50,380 --> 00:33:51,070
Darn it!

502
00:33:51,290 --> 00:33:52,890
Chita, you scum!

503
00:33:53,420 --> 00:33:54,650
You again?

504
00:34:11,060 --> 00:34:12,100
I'm going after Chita.

505
00:34:13,180 --> 00:34:14,200
He can't have gotten far.

506
00:34:14,980 --> 00:34:16,440
You go back to the station

507
00:34:16,530 --> 00:34:17,660
and get backup.

508
00:34:17,960 --> 00:34:19,060
I'll catch up with you.

509
00:34:21,990 --> 00:34:23,640
I'm not letting you go alone.

510
00:34:25,530 --> 00:34:26,840
You want to chase down Chita

511
00:34:27,520 --> 00:34:28,920
because you want to die, don't you?

512
00:34:30,700 --> 00:34:31,400
Answer me!

513
00:34:31,600 --> 00:34:32,500
What's wrong with you, James?

514
00:34:33,480 --> 00:34:34,310
What's wrong?

515
00:34:36,000 --> 00:34:37,090
We're racing against time.

516
00:34:40,690 --> 00:34:42,250
We don't know where Dr. Ji is right now.

517
00:34:43,190 --> 00:34:44,470
He could be in danger.

518
00:34:58,810 --> 00:35:00,720
That scum Chita won't hurt Dr. Ji.

519
00:35:01,500 --> 00:35:02,540
But he'll hurt you.

520
00:35:03,390 --> 00:35:04,730
He definitely will.

521
00:35:17,430 --> 00:35:18,810
And I don't want anyone hurting you.

522
00:35:28,030 --> 00:35:30,120
I can't lose someone
important to me again, Ken.

523
00:35:38,160 --> 00:35:39,220
If I let you go,

524
00:35:41,090 --> 00:35:42,260
what if you never come back?

525
00:35:45,890 --> 00:35:46,590
See?

526
00:35:53,270 --> 00:35:54,200
You know it too.

527
00:35:55,360 --> 00:35:56,660
You know it deep down.

528
00:36:00,760 --> 00:36:02,580
So why are you
choosing to leave me again?

529
00:36:07,550 --> 00:36:09,160
Don't you care how I feel?

530
00:36:30,360 --> 00:36:31,380
Do you remember that plan?

531
00:36:33,000 --> 00:36:33,960
The plan I told you about.

532
00:36:36,130 --> 00:36:37,520
I'll find the culprit

533
00:36:38,520 --> 00:36:40,650
and the murderer who killed
my father as soon as possible.

534
00:36:43,400 --> 00:36:45,080
Because I want to hurry up
and live my life with you.

535
00:36:46,700 --> 00:36:47,900
I can barely wait anymore.

536
00:36:54,590 --> 00:36:56,090
I can't do it alone, Ken.

537
00:36:58,780 --> 00:36:59,880
You have to be part of it.

538
00:38:20,530 --> 00:38:21,940
We'll go find Chita together

539
00:38:24,660 --> 00:38:26,280
and end this together, James.

540
00:39:46,070 --> 00:39:47,570
You scum! Where are you going?

541
00:39:47,960 --> 00:39:48,900
Come back!

542
00:40:29,160 --> 00:40:32,960
♪Surrounded by people all around♪

543
00:40:32,960 --> 00:40:36,800
♪Yet I'm the only one who's lonely♪

544
00:40:36,800 --> 00:40:40,040
♪I never thought I'd ever meet you♪

545
00:40:40,040 --> 00:40:43,960
♪Someone I could love with all my heart♪

546
00:40:43,960 --> 00:40:47,480
♪Only after the pain
of parting did I understand♪

547
00:40:47,480 --> 00:40:51,320
♪But this time I won't let you go♪

548
00:40:51,320 --> 00:40:54,720
♪As long as you're walking beside me♪

549
00:40:54,720 --> 00:40:59,360
♪I know just how lucky I am♪

550
00:40:59,360 --> 00:41:02,640
♪When two worlds
draw near and gently hear♪

551
00:41:02,640 --> 00:41:06,680
♪Soul's beat as one,
a voice forever clear♪

552
00:41:06,680 --> 00:41:09,040
♪I love you♪

553
00:41:09,040 --> 00:41:12,840
♪the sweetest word I know♪

554
00:41:14,720 --> 00:41:18,240
♪Each goodnight breath♪

555
00:41:18,560 --> 00:41:21,400
♪Each meaning grows♪

556
00:41:21,400 --> 00:41:28,040
♪Love weighs more than my soul can hold♪

557
00:41:28,320 --> 00:41:31,040
♪I love you♪

558
00:41:31,680 --> 00:41:39,240
♪I love you truly, heart and soul♪

559
00:41:42,680 --> 00:41:46,320
♪The love I give you is beyond measure♪

560
00:41:46,320 --> 00:41:50,000
♪More than words could ever explain♪

561
00:41:50,000 --> 00:41:53,240
♪My world is no longer empty♪

562
00:41:53,240 --> 00:41:56,880
♪You are my warmest shelter♪

563
00:41:56,880 --> 00:42:00,560
♪Now that I've found
the one I've searched for♪

564
00:42:00,560 --> 00:42:04,760
♪Our two hearts are bound,
never to part♪

565
00:42:04,760 --> 00:42:08,200
